WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.865
Apollo. To reach the Moon, predict the future.

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:14.216
First, estimate position and velocity at a known time. This state
vector starts the calculation of where gravity takes the spacecraft.

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:24.619
A forward burn adds speed and raises the orbit's far side.
Translunar injection sends Apollo from Earth orbit toward the Moon.

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:31.829
The Moon moves during flight. NASA integrated the equations of
motion to target where the Moon would be.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:44.763
Lunar gravity bends the path. A free-return trajectory leads back
toward Earth. To stay at the Moon, Apollo needed a braking burn.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:52.583
Tracking refines the prediction. Course corrections target a narrow
entry corridor, bringing Apollo home.
